                              MetalScan v1.03
                              ===============
                 Written by Ray A. Akey (AKA Heavy Metal)
                 Using the SAS/C Development System v6.55

                                    ---

changes v1.03
-------------
1. It has never been noted as so in these docs but MetalScan has been and is
   PURE and can be made resident using the following command:

      resident Pfiles:MetalScan Pfiles:MetalScan

2. Implemented the [R]ead option during browse.
3. New SLTokens added.  See the included text "token_format.readme"
4. Be sure to note the new MODCHECK program argument.  For the included
   MetalScanText.DUAL optional language text to be displayed properly, the
   DUAL argument must be used in your SCAN command if the DATES argument is
   used:

      ie.  S LANG dual MODCHECK DATES

   The .dual text prints two items per line in a "file list" sort-of look.
   The MODCHECK argument is required to insert a CR/LF just before the date
   header when single items are displayed.  For instance:

        ##  Item                             ##  Item
         2  mystuff.lha                       3  hisstuff.lha
         4  someotherstuff.lha

        ----------------------- 03-Jun-2001 ----------------------

         5  anewbatch.lha                     6. MoreNewStuff.lha
         7. evenmore.lha                      8. AndTheLast.lha

        ----------------------- 04-Jun-1994 ----------------------


   If you did not use the MODCHECK argument, the above would appear as:


        ##  Item                             ##  Item
         2  mystuff.lha                       3  hisstuff.lha
         4  someotherstuff.lha
        ----------------------- 03-Jun-2001 ----------------------

         5  anewbatch.lha                     6. MoreNewStuff.lha
         7. evenmore.lha                      8. AndTheLast.lha

        ----------------------- 04-Jun-1994 ----------------------


   NOTE the missing linefeed just before the DATE header in the above text.
        MODCHECK inserts it strategically.  Note how in the above "wrong"
        display, the linefeed is NOT needed after the 8th item and before the
        date string..

known bug: Due to the way CNet stores message authors/handles/names, if you
           use the tokens POSTERHANDLE or TOHANDLE, the message display will
           be somewhat slowed.  It is advisable to use these tokens only in
           the [R]ead message headers and text.  They will be inserted
           where YOU decide so they CAN be used in the regular scan text.
           This is only to warn you of the potential slow-down until I can
           find a way to speed it up.  Play with it and have some fun.


changes v1.02
-------------
1. Added support for alternate "MetalScanText.<string>" text.  EVERY line in
   the MetalScanText must exist in the alternate text file but does not
   have to be exactly alike.  You may use different languages, different
   SLTokens, etc,..  Your imagination is the limit.

   For example:
   If the user enters "s LANG French", then MetalScan will not attempt
   to open SYSTEXT:METALSCANTEXT.  It will attempt to use
   SYSTEXT:METALSCANTEXT.FRENCH for it's display text.

   If the user enters "s LANG 2", MetalScan will attempt to use the text
   file SYSTEXT:METALSCANTEXT.2 as it's display text.

   If the user enters "s LANG" with no other arguments, he/she is given a list
   of available alternative text files with a prompt of choice.

   You can take advantage of this for multiple language systems or to create
   what "looks" like alternate/different scan commands.

2. Fixed "Direct Access" bug where MetalScan would always display "No matching
   items".
3. Added "SAVE" argument where the user's MetalScan preferences can be saved
   as his/her default.  Currently, MetalScan saves the following argument
   preferences to mail:users/<user_ID>/MSC.PREFS

      NEW
      VERS
      DATES
      GLOBAL
      BROWSE
      LANG <alternate language/text name>

      REMEMBER: <alternate text name> refers ONLY to the extension that
                you use on the base filename METALSCANTEXT.  See changes v1.02
                item (1.) for more info.

      ie.  "s NEW TOTAL DATES SAVE" would cause MetalScan to save so that
           when the user enters "S", the arguments "NEW TOTAL DATES" will
           be automagically assumed.

           "S NOSAVE" removes the user's previously saved preferences.

changes v1.01
-------------
1. Added DATES option that, when given as an MSC argument, displays the
   DATE of the next batch of files ONCE at the beginning of the batch.
   "Batch" refers to a set of files with the same YEAR, MONTH and DATE.
   Since this change, METALSCANTEXT has now been moved from your CNET
   directory to SYSTEXT: and another line has been added to METALSCANTEXT.
   The new line is the editable text that represents the DATE displayed
   when the DATES option/argument is given by the user.

   Scan can be replaced with MetalScan in CNET:BBSMENU by replacing the text:

      Scan

   with:

      !Scan

   and adding at the end of the section where "Scan" was found:

      MSC        |{#2Pfiles:MetalScan}
      Scan~MSC DATES

   Also, SN can be aliased by simply replacing occurances of:

      SN~Scan NEW

   with:

      SN~MSC NEW DATES


   Also, MSC now has included a STOCK cnet:bbsmenu that has ONLY the MSC
   aliases installed for your convenience.  Search for "MSC" and "SCAN"
   to find the changes in the included bbsmenu.
== end of changes =====





                             ABOUT THE PROGRAM
                             =================
MetalScan is a VERY powerful replacement/companion for CNet's SCAN function
because of it's excellent configurability!

MetalScan is more powerful than CNet's built-in SCAN command in many ways.

Features: all current CNet scan options, plus the following additional
          options:

          - display/list TOTALLY configurable using Metalsoft's SLToken(tm)
            system.
          - Filesize smaller or larger than x (smaller and larger
            can be used in combination to list files in a given range of
            sizes.
          - missing items
          - total size of listed files.



                               INSTALLATION
                               ------------
   The one and only way to properly install MetalScan (hereafter called MSC)
is to add it to your BBSMENU as follows:

1. Copy MetalScan to your P-Files directory or another appropriate location.
2. Copy MetalScanText to your SYSTEXT: directory.
3. Find the end of the section in BBSMENU labeled "4; ud/base"
4. Insert a blank line right after the LAST command in that section.
5. Insert the following text on the newly inserted line:

   MSC          |#2pfiles:MetalScan}

6. Save your changes
7. Select the menuitem TEXT/MENU RELOAD in your CNet control panel.
8. Login and go into a UD/Base and enter MSC HELP.
9. Try MSC <option1> <option2> ... <optionx>
   where <optionx> is one of the options/arguments listed in the MSC HELP
   text.



          BELOW IS THE MSC TEXT WITHOUT MCI FOR YOUR CONVENIENCE
          ======================================================
Simply enter MSC (or the command that the sysop has configured) to scan items
in the current subboard.
For more control over what is listed, MetalScan allows additional command
line arguments as follows:

   HELP       This help file.
   NEW        Scan new items only. (ie. "MSC NEW")
   GLOBAL     Scans items in ALL subboards from the current one forward.
   RESET      By default, MetalScan will NOT allow you to scan NEW items
              in the current subboard twice.  Use the RESET argument to
              over-ride this restriction.
   DEBUG      For programmer/Sysop debugging.
   MISSING    Only show MISSING/OFFLINE files.
   BROWSE     Turn on interactive BROWSE mode.
   ALL        Scan/Browse all files (add the BROWSE argument for BROWSE mode).
   SIZE +/-x  List files larger or smaller than x
              ie.   "MSC SIZE +200000" lists all files larger than 200kB
                    "MSC SIZE -50000" lists all files amller than 50kB
              note: SIZE + and SIZE - can be used together to list only a
                    certain range of files based on size.
   '<text>    text beginning with a single quote is considered a file
	           pattern. Filenames and short descriptions are then checked
	           for text that matches the text.
   (ADOS)     All AmigaDOS file pattern matching is allowed also.
              ie.  "MSC sum*" will find all files with titles or comments
                   that BEGIN with the text "sum"
                   "MSC sum#?" does the same thing.
                   note that the IBM style wildcard (*) may not be available
                   unless the sysop has a commodity running that enables it.
                   "MSC *stuff*" would list all files that have titles or
                   comments containing the text "stuff".
	TOTAL      Sum and display the total size of all files listed.
	DATES      Display the file date of each new batch of files as a header.
   VERS       Display MetalScan version information (the same string that is
              displayed when a "version MetalScan" is executed in an ADos
              shell).
   LANG <x>   Use an alternate display, if available.
              if you enter the LANG argument without any other arguments, 
              MetalScan will list all available alternative displays.
              Otherwise, you must enter LANG <alternate language>

